# A MONOTONE query that still projects an unbound cell: the left
# branch of the UNION never binds ?label, and no ex: individual
# carries an rdfs:label, so every row has ?label unbound. UNION is
# monotone (each branch is, and loss can only remove rows from
# either), which is the point: it lets a test isolate the null-cell
# reason for rests_on_absence from the non-monotone-query reason.
#
# Deliberately free of every keyword on cq.rs's
# NON_MONOTONE_KEYWORDS list, INCLUDING in this comment: that scan
# reads the raw query text, comments and all, so naming a keyword
# here would set the flag and leave the test unable to fail.
PREFIX sulo: <https://w3id.org/sulo/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?o ?label WHERE {
  { <http://example.org/a> sulo:isPartOf ?o }
  UNION
  { <http://example.org/a> sulo:isPartOf ?o . ?o rdfs:label ?label }
}
